%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Deactivation is rejected when future schedules exist. Snapshot refresh is explicit, not an automatic change to sold history.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Center Manager
    participant UI as ClassForm
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as classesController
    participant S as classesService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Edit class capacity, room, sport or requirement snapshot
    UI->>API: PATCH /api/v1/classes/:id
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorize(MANAGER), validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: updateClass(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: updateClass(id, data)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Read class, future schedules, held seats, rooms and Coach expertise
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Reject capacity below retained bookings and incompatible future resources
        S->>S: refreshRequirements needs a reason and compatible room capabilities
        alt class missing or change invalidates held future schedules
            S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Persist class and supported relations after checks
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S-->>C: Updated class
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error

